WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:02.180
Class is done for today!

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:04.810
But don't slack off on your homework!

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:07.400
That's right, don't slack off!

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:08.480
Now begone!

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.030
You stayed awake today.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:15.990
If somebody could sleep through
that guy's yelling, I'd worry about him.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:17.620
Good point.

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:21.950
Have a wonderful day, everyone!

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:53.880
"Episode 8: Challenge! Part-Time Job"

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:57.760
Demiurge, I have someplace I'd like to stop.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:58.760
Sure, that's fine.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:01.600
--I'll be ready to go in just a second.
--Hey, you know...

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:03.850
Visha's been leaving
as soon as class is over, right?

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:04.720
That's right.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:07.180
She used to be with you all the time.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:10.350
Well, I'm sure she needs her space.

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:12.980
I bet you're a little lonely, though.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:16.860
Lonely? No, I don't feel lonely.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:18.570
I'd prefer you acted more like a little girl,

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:22.450
and said, "I-I'm not lonely at all!"

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:23.910
Right, Beako?

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:29.330
I'm sick of how you pass the ball straight to me
whenever the words "little girl" come up!

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.630
Don't be like that. Play along.

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.250
Would you shut up, I wonder?

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:36.340
I'd be lonely without you,
Subaru, so let's go home!

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:38.220
A sudden invitation!

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:40.680
But yeah, I don't have anything to do today.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:41.970
Let's go home.

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:42.970
What about you, Emilia?

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:45.430
Yeah, I don't have anything to do either.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:46.680
I can go with you.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:51.310
Okay, let's hit up the
butchers on the way home.

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:52.350
Hold it.

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:53.980
What is it, sis?

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:57.150
If you're going to eat croquettes,
I'm willing to go with you.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:00.860
That's just like you, to not say,
"I want to go with you."

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:01.700
Right, Beako?

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:04.120
Why do you keep asking me things, I wonder?

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:06.290
Let's go, Barusu. Hurry.

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:09.040
Okay, see you tomorrow, everyone.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:10.460
Farewell.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:12.250
See you later!

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:14.290
So you are coming, Beako?

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:17.090
--I just happened to be going
in the same direction.
--Subaru's really popular.

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:19.090
--Don't get the wrong idea.
--Yeah. He really is.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:22.590
Kazuma, let's go.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.890
I found a good explosion spot!

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:27.220
--Will you go with me?
--Sure.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:28.720
That's no fair, Megumin!

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:32.900
Kazuma was supposed to get me
a stuffed animal at the arcade.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.810
Kazuma, I told you that they're
having a sale on veggies

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:37.270
at the department store today!

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:39.030
You said you'd go with me!

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:40.940
Okay, fine.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.990
Let's just hit them all up in order.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:43.910
--♪ Explosion, explosion, lah-lah-lah! ♪

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:45.530
--See you tomorrow!
--♪ Explosion, explosion, lah-lah-lah! ♪

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:46.580
--Bye!
--♪ Explosion, explosion, lah-lah-lah! ♪

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:48.580
--Farewell!
--Wait, Kazuma!

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.830
I'm not ready to go.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:53.460
Kazuma's really popular...

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:58.380
Captain Weiss, you've been kind of down
since Valentine's Day, haven't you?

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:00.630
What should we get today?

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:03.180
Croquettes? Chicken wings?

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:05.470
Maybe even <i>menchi-katsu</i>?

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:07.220
--I can smell the lard from here...

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:09.390
--Hey, Subaru.
--I can smell the lard from here...

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:11.350
Is that...?

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:13.600
Welcome!

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:14.940
That's...

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:18.440
That'll be 240 yen!

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:19.900
Visha?

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:23.070
So that happened.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:25.660
She was working a part-time job?

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:29.700
Yeah. She's been running
out the door to get to her job.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.580
Good morning, Tanya. Subaru.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.000
Oh, morning.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.370
Morning.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:37.330
By the way, we saw Visha
in town the other day.

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:40.000
Yeah, we saw her, too.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.090
I didn't know she had a job.

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.800
You saw her, too?

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:47.800
Yes. Albedo wanted to go
to the convenience store.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:48.720
Convenience store?

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.430
Not the butchers?

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:52.180
Butchers?

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:54.270
What are you talking about?

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:55.940
What's going on here?

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:57.350
Hey, guys.

00:04:57.350 --> 00:05:00.230
We went to the department store
yesterday, and Visha was there.

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:01.650
Hold it.

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:07.910
Lt. Serebryakov was working
at the department store yesterday?

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:10.080
"Lt. Serebryakov Activity Record"

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:15.000
I've gathered you all here
to discuss our lieutenant.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.040
Let's go over what we know, I guess.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:21.090
We saw Visha working a
part-time job yesterday.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:22.210
Right, Ains?

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:24.090
Yeah, we did. What about you?

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.220
We saw it, too.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:26.590
We did, too!

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:27.680
As did we.

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:29.140
I did, too.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:30.850
We did as well.

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:31.180
"Lt. Serebryakov Activity Record"

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:34.310
So where was she working?

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:35.560
The convenience store.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.020
The department store's grocery section.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:38.100
The doughnut store.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.100
Ramen place.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:40.560
The karaoke place.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:41.820
Handicrafts store.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:43.530
Handicrafts?

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:46.990
It feels like if you got into handicrafts,
you could make something incredible...

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:47.910
It does?

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:48.860
Yeah. Really.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:51.200
Guys, we're getting off topic.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.830
I saw her in the butchers.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:56.460
--What's going on here?
--Good morning.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:59.630
What's going on, everyone?

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:01.920
Oh, Lt. Serebryakov. Actually--

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:05.340
It's almost time for class, everybody.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:09.260
Class, or as they call it in English, <i>class</i>!

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:11.720
Yeah, that's what they call it.

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:15.520
Oh, you found out I was
working part-time jobs?

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:16.890
Sorry.

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:20.520
No, it's not against the rules or anything.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.650
But we were wondering why.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:26.780
Well, actually...

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:33.030
"Special Menu"

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:38.250
I just can't stop thinking about it...

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:40.420
The special menu in the cafeteria?

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:42.290
Has anybody here ordered it?

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:43.460
I haven't.

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:45.300
It's 30,000 yen, right?

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:47.550
It's a waste to spend that on lunch.

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:49.010
Wow, I thought you were a bigger spender.

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:51.930
You can't waste money on everything.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.720
But aren't you curious?

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:55.890
It's special! Special!

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:57.390
I'm curious, sure.

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:59.270
But you're working too much.

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:03.150
Well you see, if you work
at a place, they feed you.

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:06.530
And I kept finding new things
I wanted to try, and...

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:07.820
"Convenience Store"
"Meat Bun and Onigiri Fair"

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:10.360
So, I get that.

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:13.030
But why are you working, too?

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:19.080
After hearing what she said, we got
curious about this special menu, too.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:21.210
So the others are working, too?

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:22.040
Yeah.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:23.790
Darkness and I are working here,

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:23.920
"Karaoke"

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:27.760
but Subaru's group is working at...
karaoke, I think.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:30.630
Excuse me.

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:34.050
Look! It's CZ's death voice!

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:35.970
That's no death voice!

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:37.510
But it is creepy.

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:39.770
Oh, it's the mysterious Subaru.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:41.940
You're working here, huh?

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:44.810
I'm not sure where that
nickname came from, but here.

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:46.270
Anyway, here's your order...

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:47.230
It's gone!

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:49.820
The honey toast was here
a second ago, and it's gone!

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:52.780
You think you dropped it somewhere?

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:54.370
Not a chance.

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:56.370
You'll just have to remake it.

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:59.660
Hey, you're chewing on something!

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:01.460
I have no idea what you're talking about.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:04.500
You just gulped! I heard it!

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:07.090
Subaru's taking a long time...

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:09.840
Yes, you want to extend for an hour, okay?

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:13.880
The single customer in room three
wants to extend for an hour!

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:31.940
Okay, here we go...

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:36.570
--This sound...
--What? What? What? What?

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:38.530
--Could it be...
--What? What? What? What?

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:40.290
On guard, everyone!

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:45.540
What's wrong?

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:48.540
Nothing happened.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.710
Your special menu is here!

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:54.090
It's huge!

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:56.050
Huh? The butcher?

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:57.680
He's the guy who works
at the convenience store.

00:08:57.680 --> 00:08:59.010
You mean the doughnut shop.

00:08:59.010 --> 00:08:59.890
No.

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:00.810
No. No.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:03.770
No. No. No. No. No. No. No.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:10.650
Yay!

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:19.700
It's special!

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:24.040
I guess it was only special
because of its size, huh?

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:26.250
It was surprisingly normal, huh?

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:28.170
So, what do you want to do?

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:30.590
We've got the money we earned, too, but...

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:33.460
We don't need to use it here.

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:34.300
Yup.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:37.840
Oh my god... This is just incredible!

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:43.970
How about I get you all some coffee to thank you
for putting up with my subordinate's silliness?

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:46.230
Sure. I'll take mine iced.

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:47.060
Me, too.

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:49.100
I can't drink, but I'll have some, too.

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:51.480
If you can't drink it, why do you need it?

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:53.070
Because that would be sad.

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:55.570
You can be kinda cute, huh, Ains?

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:57.530
Don't call me cute.

00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:01.830
--This is amazing!
--Visha sure eats a lot.

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:05.830
Where does it all go in
that tiny body? Tell me!

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:09.120
--She's a true glutton.
--Come on! I've gotta know!

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:10.830
Terrifying.

00:10:12.420 --> 00:11:50.787
This is great!
